==English==
{{wp|actor (disambiguation)|actor}}
{{wp|actor|actor (player)}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|acter||uncommon}}
* {{alt|en|actour||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₂eǵ-}}
{{inh+|en|enm|actour}}, from {{der|en|xno|actor}}, {{der|en|frm|actor}}, and their source, {{der|en|la|āctor||doer}}, from {{m|la|agō||to do}}. Equivalent to {{suffix|en|act|or}}. Cognate with {{cog|grc|ἄκτωρ||leader}}, from {{m|grc|ἄγω||lead, carry, convey, bring}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈak.tə/|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈæk.tɚ/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-actor.ogg|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Back ache-actor.wav|a=UK}}
* {{homophones|en|acter}}
* {{rhymes|en|æktə(ɹ)|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{head|en|noun|plural|actors|female|actress|or (nonstandard)|actoress}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete|legal}} Someone who institutes a legal suit; a [[plaintiff]] or [[complainant]]. {{defdate|13th–19th c.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Someone acting on behalf of someone else; a [[guardian]]. {{defdate|14th–18th c.}}
# Someone or something that takes part in some action; a [[doer]], an [[agent]]. {{defdate|from 15th c.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1792|author={{w|Charlotte Smith (writer)|Charlotte Smith}}|title=Desmond|publisher=Broadview|year_published=2001|page=373
|passage=Never, my dear Bethel, did the most feverish dreams of fiction produce scenes more painful, or more terrific, than the real events to which I have been an '''actor''', since the date of my last letter.}}
# A person who acts a part in a theatrical play or (later) in film or television; a dramatic performer. {{defdate|from 16th c.}}
#* {{quote-song
|en
|title=Anticipate
|album=Not So Soft
|author=w:Ani DiFranco
|year=1991
|passage=Seems like everyone's an '''actor''' / Or they're an '''actor''''s best friend / I wonder what was wrong to begin with / That they should all have to pretend}}
#* {{quote-av|en|date=Apr 2 2017|actor=w:John Oliver|title=w:Last Week Tonight with John Oliver|season=4|number=7|episode=Marijuana|network=HBO|text=Exactly. Marijuana is something we just all gradually decided is okay, like Mark Wahlberg as a serious '''actor'''. “You know what? Sure, I’ve decided I’m fine with that.”}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=2010|author=w:Peter Corris|title=Torn Apart|publisher=Allen and Unwin|page=88|text="I'm an actress -- '''actor''', as we have to say these days."}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete|Ancient Rome}} An [[advocate]] or proctor in civil courts or causes. {{defdate|16th–19th c.}}
# {{lb|en|grammar}} The [[subject]] performing the action of a [[verb]]. {{defdate|from 18th c.}}
# {{lb|en|software engineering}} The entity that performs a role (in [[use case]] [[analysis]]).

====Usage notes====
* In the sense of a person who acts in a play or film, the traditional sense of the word only applied to male actors, the term {{m|en|actress}} being used for the female counterpart.

